From 1d216249efb087480426df80b2d5149470f8d78e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:51:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 090/137] Unified: AI chat, and fix buttons in the design check

AI chat (right dock, toolbar and Model menu 'AI'): Claude, through the Agent
SDK in a separate process (AIAgentBridge.py, Python with claude-agent-sdk),
looks at the document, runs Python in FreeCAD, takes screenshots and runs
the design check. Each code the AI wants to run is shown to the user and
runs only when approved; each run is one undo step and is rolled back on an
error. Authentication is the user's own Anthropic API key, kept in the
system key store (a file only the user can read where there is none); a
hidden preference uses the local claude login instead. 'Set up the AI'
makes a venv with claude-agent-sdk and keyring.

- 'Ask AI' at the end of the actions offered next to a picked face, edge,
  sketch or part, and in the design check panel for the selected problem.
- Design check panel: 'Fix', 'Fix all that can be fixed' (one undo step).
- Menus that cannot be inserted before 'Windows' are appended with a
  warning instead of being dropped; an optional module that fails to load
  does not stop the next ones.
- Localized default labels for boxes, cylinders, drawings and more.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
